{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5Lxwdvpcgzd2dhNFkb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `addMonths` in `dates.js`, but I haven't run it. Bash was denied in this session, so I checked the change by reading it.\n\n**The bug:** `setMonth` doesn't clamp the day. Jan 31 + 1 month asked for \"Feb 31\", which rolled over to Mar 3. Any customer billed on the 29th–31st could be pushed into the following month.\n\n**The fix:** the function now does the following:\n1. Saves the original day of the month.\n2. Sets the date to the 1st, so `setMonth` can't overflow.\n3. Adds the months.\n4. Clamps the day to the last day of the target month.\n\nExpected results by hand:\n- Jan 31 + 1 → Feb 28 (or Feb 29 in a leap year)\n- Mar 31 + 1 → Apr 30\n- Jan 15 + 1 → Feb 15 (time of day kept, input not mutated)\n\n**Next steps:** I haven't checked whether any tests or callers depend on the old overflow behaviour, and I didn't add a regression test. If you can run `node -e` or your test suite, a quick check of the cases above would confirm the change. Bash may need to be allowed for that."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":935,"cache_read_input_tokens":23853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":935},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c48d3d86-749e-4358-94c6-9ec839a39e90","uuid":"9b5c9693-aac7-43c4-aed9-9915777fcfc3","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:32:02.022Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5LxkE2T3xsfiHGJPJ3"}
